description:
# Layer-by-layer optimizer (Fable design, 2026-09-27; the product owner's strategy)
Primary explorer move: fix the stack (layers the user approved) and search for the best NEXT layer, one role at a time (bass -> drums -> pad -> lead -> texture; full-mix only if the stack has none).

Validator: scripts/check-layer.py STACK_STEMS CANDIDATE_STEMS [--stack-cache F] [--json] -> {score 0-100, gates, terms, weights, findings, pairs, candidate_features}. Reuse check.py's kernel and guards.
Hard gates:
- not silent (within 18 dB of the loudest stack stem, above -40 LUFS, >=40% of beats);
- not a double (onset r<0.9 and chroma cosine<0.97 against every stack stem);
- role gate;
- tuning within 8 cents;
- stretch in [0.8,1.25] for complex/texture, [0.67,1.5] for beats.
Soft terms, as penalties in [0,1] with weights:
- clash 0.35 (the existing kernel plus chord clash);
- masking 0.15 (cosine of Bark/ERB band energy per beat, weighted by tonalness, plus register separation);
- rhythm 0.15 (onset-envelope doubling r>0.6 penalized; rewards filling the stack's quiet 1/4-beat slots up to 0.5; scaled down for pads);
- density/energy 0.10;
- artefacts 0.10 (|log2 stretch|, |shift|/7, flatness increase);
- beat alignment 0.05;
- taste 0.10 (the rating; 0.5 when unrated).
score = 100*(1 - sum w p / sum w). Diversity at finalist selection by MMR (cosine < 0.8).
Sanity checks: silent -> gate; a copy of track 1 -> gate; a semitone shift scores below a fifth shift; white noise loses.
Cache: the stack's features in renders/<stack>.features.npz, computed once per run; per-clip sidecar features keyed by manifest sha.
Pipeline: roles from cheap features -> manifest screen (loudness-weighted beat_chroma through the kernel after the solver shift; bpm best of x0.5/x1/x2 within the gate), top ~60 per role -> sidecar screen, top 12-20 -> render 8-16 bars with --stems -> check-layer -> MMR to 3 finalists -> an inner loop (gain, octave, notch, hp, warp) -> the user A/Bs.
Log the proxy-vs-render Spearman rho and recall@12 in the notebook.
Stop when the best candidate < the stack objective - 2, the density budget is exceeded, or all roles are filled with a gain < 2.
Revisit: a one-slot re-audition of earlier layers after each accepted layer (accept if > +1); a beam of 3; drop a branch more than 5 points behind.
Tonight's slice: track 1 = the Funky Nurykabe loop (8 bars, Ave House's tempo, key and chords); one role (bass if the loop lacks low energy, else pad from holds with warp texture); pool = loops + holds, screen to 60, render 12. Composite = check-stems clash 0.6 + masking 0.2 + onset r 0.2, with the silent and doubling gates. Output a ranked table and 12 mixes; the user A/Bs the top 3.
Validation: log every A/B (stack, A, B, composites, pick); target >70% agreement over 20+ pairs; fit the weights by logistic regression / Bradley-Terry at ~30 pairs.
